---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { useTranslations } from '../i18n';
import { repoFile, url } from '../lib/url.ts';
import { SITE } from '../site.config.ts';

const t = useTranslations();
---

<Base title={t('about.title')} description={t('about.description')}>
  <article class="lesson mx-auto max-w-[720px] py-8 sm:py-12">
    <h1>{t('about.title')}</h1>
    <p>
      Xtraplaytion is a playground for fitting curves. Pick a function, choose where the data lives,
      and watch neural networks and classical models learn it, live in your browser. Then see what
      they do in the gaps and beyond the data, where they have to guess.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Every model trains on your own device, in background threads of your browser. There is no
        server doing the work, and none that receives your experiments.
      </li>
      <li>
        On the processor, training uses its own math library, so the same experiment gives exactly
        the same numbers in every browser. That is why a shared link rebuilds the same race.
      </li>
      <li>
        On the graphics card (through WebGPU), training is much faster but approximate: graphics
        cards compute with fewer digits, so results can differ a little from device to device.
      </li>
      <li>
        A few heavy races come as recordings made on a graphics card, marked Recorded, so they play
        on any device. You can always train them yourself.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Free, with no ads, no subscription and no account.</li>
      <li>
        Your experiments stay in your browser. A share link keeps the whole experiment after the #
        sign of the address, the part that browsers never send to a server. The library keeps your
        saves in this browser only.
      </li>
      <li>
        One cookie, and only if you agree: if you accept in the cookie bar, Google Analytics counts
        visits. It gets the address of the page without the part after the # sign, and nothing you
        made. If you decline, nothing from Google loads at all.
      </li>
      <li>Races embedded in other sites never load analytics.</li>
    </ul>
    {SITE.analytics.enabled && (
      <p>
        <button type="button" class="xp-btn min-h-11" data-consent-open>
          {t('footer.cookies')}
        </button>
      </p>
    )}

    <h2>What you make is yours</h2>
    <p>
      Images, videos, GIFs, files and saved experiments you create here belong to you. Use and share
      them however you like, with or without credit. Exported videos carry a small Made with
      Xtraplaytion line that you can switch off. Fonts inside them keep their own open licenses.
    </p>

    <h2>Embedding</h2>
    <p>
      You may put a race from this site on your own page: open the playground, press Share, then
      Embed on a page, and paste the code. The race keeps pointing to this site and trains in each
      visitor's browser. Please do not present Xtraplaytion as your own work.
    </p>

    <h2>License</h2>
    <p>
      Xtraplaytion is source-available, not open source. The source code is public under the{' '}
      <a href={repoFile('LICENSE')}>KFA Source-Available License 1.0</a>. The components it builds
      on and their licenses are listed in the{' '}
      <a href={url('THIRD_PARTY.md')}>third-party notices</a>. The source lives on{' '}
      <a href={SITE.repoUrl}>GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
